1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,170
Ollie: Good morning, Pip! The water is so calm today.

2
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:09,420
Pip: Ollie, look! They are all linked up.

3
00:00:09,820 --> 00:00:15,210
Ollie: They're holding hands, even while they sleep!

4
00:00:16,710 --> 00:00:19,070
Ollie: Why do otters hold hands?

5
00:00:21,710 --> 00:00:24,330
Ollie: Let's find out!

6
00:00:55,830 --> 00:01:01,600
Ollie: Maybe they're cold! Or maybe they're best friends!

7
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:04,430
Pip: Ollie, I think Bean is floating away.

8
00:01:10,930 --> 00:01:16,310
Ollie: Oh no. I swam off without you, Bean.

9
00:01:22,810 --> 00:01:26,470
Pip: Look. Now you're not drifting at all.

10
00:01:26,870 --> 00:01:30,160
Ollie: Hmm. Is that why otters hold hands?

11
00:01:31,660 --> 00:01:33,170
Pip: Even the baby is holding on.

12
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:40,810
Gus: Hold hands? That sounds slow. I've got a faster way!

13
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:44,850
Pip: Gus, your faster ways always go wrong.

14
00:01:46,350 --> 00:01:49,670
Gus: Not this time! I'll just lie down and stay right here.

15
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:55,340
Ollie: You won't hold on to anything?

16
00:01:55,740 --> 00:01:59,560
Gus: Nope! Naps are easy. Watch me.

17
00:02:06,060 --> 00:02:08,180
Pip: What if we try it the careful way?

18
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:14,760
Ollie: Good idea, Pip. Let's watch Gus first. Then we ask Gran Mari.

19
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:32,330
Pip: Ollie, he's drifting away!

20
00:02:35,350 --> 00:02:39,520
Ollie: Gus! Gus, wake up! You're floating away!

21
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:44,520
Gus: Hey! Where did everybody go?

22
00:02:46,020 --> 00:02:48,110
Ollie: Did you float away, Gus?

23
00:02:48,510 --> 00:02:52,730
Gus: No! I went for a swim. On purpose!

24
00:02:53,130 --> 00:02:55,790
Pip: But you were asleep.

25
00:02:57,290 --> 00:03:02,240
Gus: I was swimming in my sleep. Very fast. Everyone does it.

26
00:03:03,740 --> 00:03:08,300
Ollie: The water moved you, and nothing held you.

27
00:03:08,700 --> 00:03:11,750
Gus: It was only a little bit. It doesn't count!

28
00:03:17,250 --> 00:03:21,410
Ollie: We need help. Let's ask Gran Mari.

29
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:31,350
Gran Mari: Well now, a damp seagull and a worried otter. What's all this?

30
00:03:32,850 --> 00:03:37,020
Ollie: Gran Mari, why do otters hold hands?

31
00:03:38,520 --> 00:03:45,650
Gran Mari: Oh, that is a good question, Ollie. Let's find out together.

32
00:03:47,150 --> 00:03:54,780
Gran Mari: This bowl is a pretend sea. These leaves are pretend otters.

33
00:03:56,280 --> 00:04:04,850
Gran Mari: This string is pretend paws. Watch the water, and watch closely.

34
00:04:06,350 --> 00:04:10,900
Ollie: They're drifting! The loose ones are drifting apart!

35
00:04:12,400 --> 00:04:16,040
Pip: The tied leaves stay together!

36
00:04:17,540 --> 00:04:27,620
Gran Mari: The sea is always moving, even when the otters sleep. So they hold paws, and nothing pulls them apart.

37
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:32,120
Gus: So if I'd held on to something, I wouldn't have drifted?

38
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:38,740
Gran Mari: Well now, what do you think happens next?

39
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:46,780
Ollie: The loose leaves keep drifting, and the tied leaves stay close!

40
00:04:58,280 --> 00:05:08,840
Ollie: Try it at home! Fill a bowl with water. Float four leaves on it. Tie two leaves together with a soft string.

41
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:17,890
Ollie: Now swirl the water gently. Watch the loose leaves drift apart. Watch the tied leaves stay together.

42
00:05:24,390 --> 00:05:28,570
Ollie: Gus, come float with us. There's room.

43
00:05:30,070 --> 00:05:35,250
Gus: I fibbed before. I wasn't swimming. I was drifting.

44
00:05:35,650 --> 00:05:37,470
Gus: I'm sorry I said it didn't count.

45
00:05:37,870 --> 00:05:40,120
Ollie: Thanks for telling us the truth, Gus.

46
00:05:57,320 --> 00:05:59,350
Bean: Hold!

47
00:06:01,320 --> 00:06:05,980
Gus: Phew! I'm not going anywhere. Thanks, friends.

48
00:06:07,480 --> 00:06:09,610
Pip: We stayed together all by ourselves.

49
00:06:17,480 --> 00:06:21,200
Ollie: Time for my Wonder Pocket! Three things we learned.

50
00:06:27,740 --> 00:06:32,760
Ollie: One. The sea is always moving, even at night.

51
00:06:34,260 --> 00:06:39,660
Ollie: Two. Otters hold paws so they do not drift apart.

52
00:06:41,160 --> 00:06:45,330
Ollie: Three. Holding on keeps friends together.

53
00:06:46,830 --> 00:06:50,870
Ollie: And one kind thing to try today. Hold a friend's hand.

54
00:06:52,860 --> 00:06:57,390
Gus: Bye, everybody! Next time, I'll hold on too!
